    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29089" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῠσ-ίᾱτος</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῠσ-ίητος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ι], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span></span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hard to heal</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κληΐς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Art.</u>
					14
				</span></i>
			 (
				Comp.
			), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Cass.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				1
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακὸν δ.</span> an ill
				<i>that none can cure</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				1103
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀργή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Med.</u>
					520
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νόσημα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					916a
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.40
			</span></i>, al.; of persons, <i>implacable</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Them.
				<u>Or.</u>
				15.192c
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τως</span>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, μόριον πεπονθὸς δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					18(2).273
				</span></i>
			.</div>
